# Elements

### Projection Alpha Scheme

Vocabulary for projection normalization checks.

#### Metadata
  * type: concept-scheme
  * concept_base: https://example.test/projection-alpha
  * concept_prefix: pa
---

### Projection Child

A child with local, cross-scheme and external relationships.

#### Mappings
  * exactMatch: <https://external.example/Exact>
  * closeMatch: <https://external.example/Close>

#### Metadata
  * type: concept

#### Relations
  * derivedFrom: [Projection Alpha Scheme](#projection-alpha-scheme)
  * broader: [Projection Parent](#projection-parent)
  * related: [Projection Peer](#projection-peer)
  * related: [Projection Remote](#projection-remote)
  * exactMatch: [Projection Remote](#projection-remote)
  * closeMatch: [Projection Remote](#projection-remote)
---

### Projection Isolated

An isolated concept still has its own RDF description.

#### Metadata
  * type: concept

#### Relations
  * derivedFrom: [Projection Alpha Scheme](#projection-alpha-scheme)
---

### Projection Parent

A parent with a reciprocal authored taxonomy link.

#### Metadata
  * type: concept

#### Relations
  * derivedFrom: [Projection Alpha Scheme](#projection-alpha-scheme)
  * narrower: [Projection Child](#projection-child)
---

### Projection Peer

An association declared consistently in both directions.

#### Metadata
  * type: concept

#### Relations
  * derivedFrom: [Projection Alpha Scheme](#projection-alpha-scheme)
  * related: [Projection Child](#projection-child)
---

### Projection Beta Scheme

Separate namespace for cross-scheme association checks.

#### Metadata
  * type: concept-scheme
  * concept_base: https://example.test/projection-beta
  * concept_prefix: pb
---

### Projection Remote

A concept linked from a different scheme without reciprocal declarations.

#### Metadata
  * type: concept

#### Relations
  * derivedFrom: [Projection Beta Scheme](#projection-beta-scheme)
---
